{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mpas_mesh_level0",
    "description": "MPAS exemplar mesh data, icosahedral level 0 on the unit sphere (R = 1; multiply lengths by R and areas by R^2 for a physical sphere): 12 Voronoi cells, 30 edges, 20 vertices — the spherical Voronoi diagram of the 12 icosahedron vertices (12 pentagonal cells; the dual dodecahedron). This is mesh DATA, not a library entry: a section-4.7 subsystem file (one model, no dynamics) whose observed variables carry the connectivity and geometry as literal `const` arrays (esm-spec 4.2 `const`; the document-literal CONST-connectivity convention of ESS tests/valid/aggregate/edge_enumeration_area_eff.esm and tests/valid/geometry/intersect_polygon_planar_ode.esm). Conventions (MPAS / Ringler et al. 2010, all ids 1-based): cellsOnEdge[e] = [c1, c2] with the positive edge normal pointing from c1 to c2; verticesOnEdge[e] = [v1, v2] with the positive tangent from v1 to v2 satisfying t = k x n (k = outward radial), so traversing v1->v2 runs counterclockwise around the cell the normal leaves; edgeSignOnCell[i][k] = +1 where the positive normal of edgesOnCell[i][k] is outward from cell i (i = c1), -1 otherwise; edgesOnCell rows list each cell's edges in counterclockwise order viewed from outside the sphere, zero-padded to maxEdges (padding slots are never dereferenced: the ragged edges_of_cell iteration is bounded by nEdgesOnCell[i]). Geometry: cell centers are the generators, mesh vertices are the circumcenters of the Delaunay triangles, dvEdge/dcEdge are great-circle arc lengths, areaCell is the spherical-polygon area (sum of signed triangle excesses; the areaCell values sum to 4*pi to < 1e-12). Derivation is exactly reproducible from the golden-ratio icosahedron (0, +/-1, +/-phi) by circumcenter duality; verified at authoring time: Delaunay empty-circumcircle for every triangle, opposite edgeSignOnCell on the two cells of every edge, and the discrete div-of-curl telescoping identity sum_k sign[i][k]*(eta[v2]-eta[v1]) == 0 exactly for arbitrary integer vertex fields eta. WIDENED CONTRACT (2026-07, regridding wave): latVertex/lonVertex/verticesOnCell added so cell polygon rings are derivable in-document (the conservative regridder consumes [cells, maxEdges, 2] lon-lat vertex rings; see grids/mpas/grid.esm mpas_cell_rings_deg). Derived from THIS FILE's committed bytes by the vertex-duality extension of the original pipeline: each mesh vertex is the circumcenter of its three adjacent generators (adjacency from verticesOnEdge + cellsOnEdge, positions from latCell/lonCell, sign chosen toward the generators), and verticesOnCell[i][k] is the vertex shared by the consecutive CCW edges edgesOnCell[i][k] and edgesOnCell[i][k+1]. Re-verified from the serialized bytes at authoring time: every vertex has exactly 3 incident edges and 3 adjacent cells and sits equidistant from its three generators to < 1e-12 rad; the derived vertex positions reproduce the committed dvEdge great-circle lengths to <= 3.3e-16 rad and the committed areaCell spherical ring areas to <= 4.4e-16 sr; every derived ring is CCW-positive and the compensated ring-area total differs from 4*pi by 0.0e+00.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:mesh-data",
      "family:mpas",
      "mesh:icosahedral_level0",
      "sphere:unit"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Ringler, T., Thuburn, J., Klemp, J. B., & Skamarock, W. C. (2010). A unified approach to energy conservation and potential vorticity dynamics for arbitrarily-structured C-grids. Journal of Computational Physics, 229(9), 3065-3090."
      }
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "cells": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 12
    },
    "edges": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 30
    },
    "vertices": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 20
    },
    "maxEdges": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 5
    },
    "edge_ends": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 2
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "MpasMeshLevel0": {
      "variables": {
        "nEdgesOnCell": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "cells"
          ],
          "description": "Edges (= vertices = neighbors) of each cell: the offsets keyed factor of the grid's ragged edges_of_cell index set."
        },
        "edgesOnCell": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "cells",
            "maxEdges"
          ],
          "description": "Edge ids around each cell, counterclockwise viewed from outside, zero-padded to maxEdges: the values keyed factor of the grid's ragged edges_of_cell index set."
        },
        "edgeSignOnCell": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "cells",
            "maxEdges"
          ],
          "description": "Outward-normal sign of edgesOnCell[i][k] with respect to cell i: +1 where cellsOnEdge[e][1] == i, -1 where cellsOnEdge[e][2] == i; 0 in never-dereferenced padding slots."
        },
        "cellsOnEdge": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "edges",
            "edge_ends"
          ],
          "description": "The two cells sharing each edge; the positive edge normal points from cellsOnEdge[e][1] to cellsOnEdge[e][2]."
        },
        "verticesOnEdge": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "edges",
            "edge_ends"
          ],
          "description": "The two vertices bounding each edge, ordered so the positive tangent (v1 -> v2) equals k x n (k = outward radial, n = positive edge normal)."
        },
        "dvEdge": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "rad",
          "shape": [
            "edges"
          ],
          "description": "Edge length: great-circle arc between verticesOnEdge[e][1] and verticesOnEdge[e][2] on the unit sphere."
        },
        "dcEdge": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "rad",
          "shape": [
            "edges"
          ],
          "description": "Cell-center spacing: great-circle arc between cellsOnEdge[e][1] and cellsOnEdge[e][2] on the unit sphere (the dual-edge length used by gradient rules)."
        },
        "areaCell": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "sr",
          "shape": [
            "cells"
          ],
          "description": "Spherical (Voronoi) area of each cell on the unit sphere; sums to 4*pi over the closed mesh."
        },
        "latCell": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "rad",
          "shape": [
            "cells"
          ],
          "description": "Latitude of each cell center (generator)."
        },
        "lonCell": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "rad",
          "shape": [
            "cells"
          ],
          "description": "Longitude of each cell center (generator), in (-pi, pi]."
        },
        "latVertex": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "rad",
          "shape": [
            "vertices"
          ],
          "description": "Latitude of each mesh vertex (Delaunay-triangle circumcenter): the circumcenter of the vertex's three adjacent generators, derived from this file's committed latCell/lonCell + verticesOnEdge + cellsOnEdge by circumcenter duality (see the file description's provenance note). With verticesOnCell this makes the cell polygon rings derivable in-document for conservative regridding."
        },
        "lonVertex": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "rad",
          "shape": [
            "vertices"
          ],
          "description": "Longitude of each mesh vertex (Delaunay-triangle circumcenter), in (-pi, pi]; same derivation and use as latVertex."
        },
        "verticesOnCell": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "cells",
            "maxEdges"
          ],
          "description": "Vertex ids around each cell, counterclockwise viewed from outside, zero-padded to maxEdges: verticesOnCell[i][k] is the vertex SHARED by the consecutive CCW edges edgesOnCell[i][k] and edgesOnCell[i][k+1 (cyclic over nEdgesOnCell[i])]. On a closed MPAS mesh every cell has exactly as many vertices as edges, so nEdgesOnCell doubles as the per-cell vertex count and no separate offsets factor is needed; padding slots are 0 and are never dereferenced (bound iteration by nEdgesOnCell[i], or clamp the gather with min(k, nEdgesOnCell[i]) as the grid's ring template does, which pads the derived ring by repeating the last real vertex -- a form the polygon_intersection_area kernels accept value-identically)."
        }
      },
